# Try the API from VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, start the API
# (Terminal → Run Task… → api: run), then click "Send Request" above any request.
# Development sign-in: change @me to act as someone else (ids are in the table at the end).

@api = http://localhost:5011/api/v1
@me = 6

### Who am I?
GET {{api}}/me
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}

### Create a defect (as Elyse). Unassigned, so it starts as New and Ken is emailed.
# @name created
POST {{api}}/tickets
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Defect",
  "applicationId": 19,
  "title": "Mileage total doubles when a trip is edited",
  "description": "Editing a submitted trip adds the new mileage to the old amount.",
  "endUserName": "Diane Cole, Membership",
  "stepsToReproduce": "1. Open an expense report\n2. Edit a mileage trip\n3. Look at the total",
  "expectedResult": "The total reflects the new distance",
  "actualResult": "Old and new amounts are added together",
  "environment": "Production",
  "severity": "High",
  "priority": "P2High"
}

### The ticket just created
@number = {{created.response.body.number}}
GET {{api}}/tickets/{{number}}
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}

### Ken triages it: assign to Max in one step (Max is emailed)
POST {{api}}/tickets/{{number}}/transitions
X-Dev-User-Id: 11
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toStatusId": 3, "assigneeId": 1 }

### Max starts work
POST {{api}}/tickets/{{number}}/transitions
X-Dev-User-Id: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toStatusId": 4 }

### Max comments and @mentions Elyse (Elyse is emailed)
POST {{api}}/tickets/{{number}}/comments
X-Dev-User-Id: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "@Elyse Orris fixed in Test, please retest." }

### Max sends it to testing (Elyse, the reporter, is emailed)
POST {{api}}/tickets/{{number}}/transitions
X-Dev-User-Id: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toStatusId": 5, "comment": "The edit now replaces the old distance." }

### Elyse verifies, then closes it
POST {{api}}/tickets/{{number}}/transitions
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toStatusId": 6 }

###
POST {{api}}/tickets/{{number}}/transitions
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toStatusId": 7 }

### Everything that changed, newest first
GET {{api}}/tickets/{{number}}/history
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}

### Open tickets, most recently updated first
GET {{api}}/tickets?view=open&sort=updated
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}

### Search by number or words
GET {{api}}/tickets?view=all&search=mileage
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}

### Status ids: 1 New, 2 Triaged, 3 Assigned, 4 In Progress, 5 Ready for Test,
### 6 Verified, 7 Closed, 8 Reopened, 9 Won't Fix
### People: 1 Max, 2 Bobby, 3 Hue, 4 Shyamal, 5 Michael, 6 Elyse, 7 Josh,
### 8 Val, 9 Jeff, 10 Greg, 11 Ken
